WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.020
To stop Academia's evil plans,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.770
my teacher, Yusyo Sakaki, 
crossed dimensions to come here.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.420
He decided to speak directly 
to the Professor.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.030
I must get him to the Professor, 
no matter what.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.830
With that in mind, we boarded a boat.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.340
But Dennis, an Academia 
pursuer, blocked our way.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.630
I'll take that duel.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.440
Kaito!

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.640
Who are you, coming out of nowhere?

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.570
Go, Neo Galaxy-Eyes...

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.110
Terrifying Cipher Stream!

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.880
With Xyz Dimension duelist Kaito's 
help, we struck down Dennis,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.420
learned the kidnapped Ruri and Rin's location,

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.790
and successfully infiltrated Academia.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.400
At last, we meet again, Mr. Sakaki.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.700
I won't let you leave me behind, 
like you did three years ago.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:59.170
I just didn't want to cause you more trouble.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.830
Academia has already become too large.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.780
If we want to destroy them, we—

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.250
Destroy them?

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.450
Can you do that?

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.730
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:24.400
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.180
Their dragons call to each other,

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.640
almost as if seeking one another.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.970
The Glorious Mechanical Dragon

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.340
I'll turn all five of you into cards together.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.560
Yuya?

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.780
I won't let you!

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.010
Asuka!

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.500
That's it... I can use that.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.600
Get going, quickly!

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.460
Hurry!

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:46.740
Layra!

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.320
Such a shame, Sora Shiunin.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:07.120
That fence interferes with duel disk functions,

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.490
so you'll have to watch from there.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:13.970
I thought I'd get you together, but I 
guess you'll do, on your own.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.030
We met before, so I investigated you...

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.980
When you were at Academia, you were 
a strict honor student, weren't you?

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:29.450
You crushed every boy who came after you.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:34.720
Getting to duel an honor student 
like you, and turn you into a card...

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.290
I just can't wait.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:39.630
Who is that boy?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.200
He looks like your son, 
but he's probably Joeri.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.110
Joeri?

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:45.770
Sir, please go!

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.460
I'll hold off Joeri.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.700
So hurry!

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.720
You're the only one who can 
persuade the Professor!

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.250
Understood! We're going now!

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.080
Aw, they left...

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.650
But, ah well.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.460
I just need to beat you and go after them.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.660
I won't let you stop them!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.960
Oh, so very scary.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.430
Hey, is this familiar?

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.930
Th-That's...

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.280
Yes...

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.930
It's the special deck supplied 
to honor students like you.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.860
I'm sure you know all the cards in it.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.280
Incidentally, this is the deck I normally use.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.910
Well? Which deck should I beat you with?

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.820
Are you mocking me?

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:39.350
Come at me honorably, with the deck 
to which you're accustomed!

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.020
I thought you'd say that...

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:47.190
So I'll go with the honor 
student deck, not my own!

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.630
Then, let's get started.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:58.730
Duel!

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.240
I'll take the first turn.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:05.380
I activate Ritual Spell Machine 
Angel Absolute Ritual!

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:19.370
And I tribute Level 5 Cyber Tutubon 
in my hand to Ritual Summon!

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:22.230
Angel of light with the power of healing,

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:25.000
bring comfort with your beautiful form.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.360
And come to Earth!

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:41.320
Level 5 Cyber Angel Natasha!

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:50.080
The turn Cyber Tutubon is used as a 
component in a Ritual Summon,

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.800
I can add one Ritual Spell from 
my graveyard to my hand.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.910
I add Machine Angel Absolute Ritual!

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.570
This card has one additional effect.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:02.730
I activate it!

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:07.270
By returning Level 5 Cyber Tutubon 
from my graveyard to my hand,

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:08.870
I can Ritual Summon once more.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:11.980
I summon another Natasha!

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:18.060
Once per turn, Natasha can choose 
one monster on my side of the field,

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:22.020
and recover my life points 
by half of its attack points.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.020
What?

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:29.730
You recover a little life, put out two 
1000-defense-point monsters,

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:30.460
and you're done?

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:32.760
Having a Natasha on my field

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:38.040
negates attacks against all Cyber 
monsters other than itself.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.420
Having two monsters with that 
same effect on the field

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.980
will keep him from attacking!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.480
That's right.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.980
I end my turn.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.510
I see.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.820
You've skillfully established 
your defenses, then...

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.950
I'll have to work hard, too.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.670
Now, it's my turn.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:59.660
Here's my first draw from 
the honor student deck!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.100
Hang on a minute.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.570
What? You really don't 
know that deck at all?

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:11.450
No...

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:13.000
Oh, I see.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.080
I should probably use this.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.380
I activate Continuous Spell 
Ancient Gear Fortress.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.370
And now...

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:27.050
I activate spell card Ancient Gear Catapult.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.020
Now, when I have no monsters 
on my side of the field,

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:37.000
Ancient Gear Catapult can destroy one 
faceup card on my side of the field?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.730
Then, I destroy Ancient Gear Fortress.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.870
He destroyed his Continuous 
Spell immediately?

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.470
It's because you're using an unfamiliar deck.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:48.360
No, I didn't make a mistake.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.640
When a card is destroyed 
by Ancient Gear Catapult,

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:56.050
I can Special Summon Ancient 
Gear Gadget from my deck!

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:02.250
And when Ancient Gear Fortress is destroyed,

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:06.490
it lets me Special Summon 
Ancient Gear Wyvern!

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:13.870
Oh, and when Ancient Gear Wyvern 
is Normal or Special Summoned,

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:18.130
I can add an Ancient Gear 
card, other than this one,

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:20.350
from my deck to my hand.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.970
Let's see, then...

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:24.710
Which should I pick?

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.800
Oh? What's this?

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.680
Hang on, can I bring out my 
trump card like this?

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.080
Trump card?

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.920
It must be that one.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.390
All right, here we go...

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:42.700
Once per turn, Ancient Gear Gadget 
can be treated as a Gadget monster.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:46.600
I tribute Ancient Gear Gadget, 
acting as a Red Gadget,

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.840
along with Ancient Gear Wyvern, 
to Tribute Summon!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:57.030
Come out, Level 9 Ancient 
Gear Reactor Dragon!

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.830
Look! I really brought it out!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.010
I told you I didn't make a mistake.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:07.040
There's no way he can Tribute Summon

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.450
the trump card of an honor 
student's special deck...

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:10.490
Damn him.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:11.770
Battle!

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.730
Reactor Dragon attacks Natasha!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.930
Natasha's effect!

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.920
When another Cyber monster, 
besides it, is on the field,

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.140
it negates attacks against itself.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.500
Oh, I forgot!

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:32.800
Actually, it says that when Reactor Dragon 
attacks, it negates all monster,

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.880
spell, and trap effects until the 
end of your Damage Step...

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.840
And it looks like it has one more effect.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:45.360
When it's Tribute Summoned 
using an Ancient Gear,

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.430
then when attacking defense-position 
monsters, it deals piercing damage!

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.710
Using an unfamiliar deck so well...

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.320
I really must be a prodigy!

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:04.650
Oh, but my turn isn't over yet.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:08.460
When Reactor Dragon is Tribute 
Summoned using a Gadget,

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:10.490
it can attack twice.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:15.420
Oh, but as an honor student yourself,

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:17.890
I'm sure you knew that.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:19.020
On that note,

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:21.860
Reactor Dragon attacks Natasha!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.360
And it deals piercing damage.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:33.490
Oh, how frustrating...

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:36.660
If I could attack once more, I could end it...

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.110
Ah, well.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.800
We'll have to save some fun for next time.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.840
I set one card and end my turn.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.250
Now, it's your turn.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.720
I'm itching to go again, so finish fast, okay?

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:55.690
Hurry. Hurry. Hurry. Hurry.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.160
Hurry. Hurry.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.160
Hurry... Hurry...

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.640
Hurry, hurry, hurry...

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:02.800
You!

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.360
There should be a girl named 
Yuzu around here.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.500
Have you seen her?

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:16.310
Hurry... Hurry... Hurry...

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.770
I will not let it end this way...

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.420
My turn!

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:27.890
I activate the effect of 
Natasha in my graveyard.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:32.460
By banishing one Cyber Angel, other than it,

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.870
I can Special Summon one Natasha!

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:42.040
Its effect lets me take control 
of one monster on your field!

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.030
What?

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:46.740
All right!

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:49.180
She stole his 3000-attack-point dragon!

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:50.680
How cruel!

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.690
You don't just steal students from Academia!

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:56.370
You'll steal my monster, too?!

00:12:56.370 --> 00:13:00.380
You're the one who stole our 
precious comrades from us.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.740
Now, you'll feel the pain of something 
precious being stolen from you!

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.430
Something precious?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:08.630
Natasha's monster effect!

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:10.010
Once per turn,

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.990
I can add half the attack points 
of one monster on the field

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.010
to my life points.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:19.340
I choose Ancient Gear Reactor Dragon!

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:23.550
Reactor Dragon can attack twice.

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:26.820
If she can deal 3000 damage twice...

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.050
Battle.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.550
I attack you directly with Ancient 
Gear Reactor Dra—

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:36.290
In that instant, I activate my trap 
card Unfinished Ancient Gear!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:43.350
It allows me to Special Summon Ancient 
Gear Golem in defense position,

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.860
ignoring its summon requirements!

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:52.240
But the effect halves the 
attack and defense points

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:54.880
of the monster it Special Summoned.

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:56.570
Still struggling?

00:13:56.570 --> 00:14:01.020
Then, I attack Ancient Gear 
Golem with Reactor Dragon!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:07.770
Monsters Special Summoned with 
Unfinished Ancient Gear

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:09.930
cannot be destroyed by battle this turn.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.530
But you take the piercing damage!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:18.430
And the second attack!

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.400
Go, Reactor Dragon!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.880
You're tough...

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.670
But I still have a trump card!

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:34.680
If it's Fusion, I won't let you use it.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:40.370
I also used to believe 
Academia to be righteous.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:42.790
But now that I know the truth,

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.160
I won't let anyone else be turned into a card.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.930
Academia must go.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.570
I am determined to see that happen.

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.400
So I won't use this ever again.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.170
I won't let you use it, either.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:02.810
I send spell card Polymerization 
from my hand to the graveyard,

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:05.250
to activate Continuous Spell 
Fusion Destruction!

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:07.690
Fusion Destruction?!

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:14.760
I can banish up to three "Fusion" or 
"Polymerization" cards in your deck.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:18.660
And for each, I deal you 
300 points of damage.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.400
All three?

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.810
You haven't used a single 
Polymerization in this duel.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:28.200
Which means they must all be in your deck.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.640
Now, banish them!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:39.550
And take a total of 900 points of damage.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.380
I now end my turn.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.810
How could you do this?

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:52.160
Stealing monsters from me...

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.540
Even stealing Fusion from me...

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.660
All this time, this is the 
way it's been for us.

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:00.140
We've had allies stolen and turned into cards.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:02.580
It's been hard on us.

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.840
So many people in the world feel that way!

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.480
The pain of precious things 
being taken from you...

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.780
Well? Do you feel it now?

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.250
Precious things...

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:18.460
It seems you do understand.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:22.580
Yeah, I didn't think it would be this painful.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:29.500
Now that you understand that pain, 
perhaps we can be friends.

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:32.800
If you have courage,

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.440
you can break free from Academia.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.680
Break free from Academia?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.510
Ever since I can remember, 
I've been an Academia student.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:48.390
I had no family. I had no friends.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:52.320
My only interaction with 
others was during duels.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.600
I enjoyed beating my opponents in duels.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.800
But...

00:16:58.110 --> 00:17:00.260
It seems I was hated for my strength.

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:03.000
Soon, they stopped talking to me entirely...

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:08.140
Then a man calling himself the 
Professor approached me.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:12.680
He said that when the 
Aquaria Project started,

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.970
I could duel as much as I wanted.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.280
I could even turn those I beat into cards.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.420
I had so much fun...

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:23.560
The more people I turned into cards,

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.740
the more pleased the Professor was.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:29.820
But I don't care about that anymore.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:35.530
I turn people into cards because 
I, myself, enjoy it!

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.500
And I'll keep doing it!

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.090
Wait a minute!

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.660
If you keep doing that,

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:44.010
you'll never make any friends!

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.500
If you turn everyone into cards, 
everyone will be gone.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.770
You'll be all alone in the world!

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.580
Me, alone in the world?

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.860
Sounds good...

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:57.960
That would mean that I was the strongest!

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:02.330
Now, let's continue...

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:04.630
My turn!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.370
I activate my spell card 
Ancient Gear Workshop!

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:12.750
I return one Ancient Gear card 
from my graveyard to my hand.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:17.300
I return Ancient Gear Wyvern 
to my hand and summon it.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.980
When Ancient Gear Wyvern is 
Normal or Special Summoned,

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:27.550
I can add one Ancient Gear card, 
aside from that one,

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.920
from my deck to my hand.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.900
I add Ancient Gear Box to my hand.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.570
And I send it to the graveyard...

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:41.320
To activate Quick-Play Spell 
Super Polymerization!

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:43.900
Super Polymerization?!

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:46.120
Why do you have that card?

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:48.340
That card shouldn't be in that deck!

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:51.000
Why do you think?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.440
I put it into the deck, of course!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.840
Wait, you really thought I was using the deck,

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:00.080
not knowing what was in it?

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:04.480
Incidentally, from the start, 
that card was in my hand.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:07.390
So you couldn't have banished it from my deck.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:08.790
From the start...

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:11.320
You tricked me!

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.720
You really are such an honor student.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:18.070
Stupidly straightforward!

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:22.480
Super Polymerization lets me use

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:26.280
Fusion components from my field, 
as well as from yours!

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:31.750
I'm going to be sacrificing that 
monster that betrayed me.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:36.280
B-But Continuous Spell Fusion Destruction 
prevents the activation of—

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.590
It's no use!

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:43.590
Effects cannot be activated to 
prevent Super Polymerization.

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:49.800
I fuse Ancient Gear Wyvern, 
Ancient Gear Golem,

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:55.480
and Ancient Gear Reactor Dragon 
on your side of the field!

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.580
Giant of antiquity, dragon who 
flies through the heavens,

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.790
dragon who shines in the abyss...

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:06.220
Become one and show your incredible power!

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.420
Fusion Summon!

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:14.780
Come out, Level 10, 
Ultimate Ancient Gear Golem!

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.760
4400 attack points?

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:25.140
Sorry, but we can't be friends.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.110
From the beginning, you never wanted that!

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:35.810
Battle! Ultimate Ancient Gear 
Golem attacks Natasha!

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:40.490
Ultimate Ancient Gear Golem 
deals piercing damage!

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.680
This ends now!

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:58.040
I have a need to turn people into cards.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.000
It's as vital as breath.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:04.440
Thanks to you, I have a dream now, as well.

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:09.250
A dream to turn all the people of the world...

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:11.850
no, of all dimensions into cards.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.390
You...

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:20.610
No!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.070
Thank you, honor student Asuka.

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:30.530
Next up...

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.390
Huh? How?

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.740
Oh, I forgot to mention...

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:40.680
I can work this system.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:44.350
I was just pretending to be trapped.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:49.450
It isn't fun without an audience, you see.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:52.520
You...

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.600
Well, time for your execution,

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:57.390
Sora Shiunin!

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:02.100
The student named Yuzu is up ahead, 
in the experimental tower.

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:03.740
Thanks!

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:10.500
Yuzu!

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:52.280
You're safe, Ruri.

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:54.780
Ruri, Kurosaki's little sister...

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:56.550
Duel me, Yuya Sakaki.

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.020
I shall turn you into a card.

00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:00.640
Turn us into cards?

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:02.250
They're totally in their power!

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.970
Yeah, Academia must be behind this!

00:24:04.970 --> 00:24:05.720
Remember!

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:11.130
You're the one who taught me that 
duels are meant to bring smiles!

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:15.170
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Reborn Phantom Knights.

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:17.620
The fun is only getting started!
